  "description": "OptunaSharp's LightGBM integration (a .NET port of Optuna's optuna.integration.lightgbm / optuna_integration.lightgbm), backed by ML.NET's native LightGBM. LightGBMTuner / LightGBMTunerCV (and the train() drop-in): the stepwise LightGBM hyperparameter tuner — feature_fraction, num_leaves, bagging, regularization, min_child_samples in a fixed order — whose Optuna-driven search (GridSampler / TPESampler) is a faithful, oracle-validated port, with training bridged to ML.NET's native LightGBM (a Phase 6 adapter; inject ILightGbmTrainer for a different engine). Also ships EXPERIMENTAL / off-label gradient-boosted-tree importance backends (LightGbmFanovaImportanceEvaluator, LightGbmMeanDecreaseImpurityImportanceEvaluator): Optuna's importance uses only scikit-learn's RandomForestRegressor (bagging), so fANOVA/MDI over a LightGBM booster is a non-standard quantity with NO value-parity to Optuna — prefer the canonical evaluators in Core. Also ships LightGBMPruningCallback (the Phase-6 port of optuna_integration.lightgbm.LightGBMPruningCallback): the metric / valid-name / report-interval lookup + the study-direction consistency check + report → should-prune → TrialPruned, fed the per-iteration evaluation log from your loop (ML.NET's LightGBM exposes no managed per-iteration hook). Part of the SciSharp STACK.",
